    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Allan Chatel",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111039360205166571870/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocICcYYD3PdJfE-AFZxiDZqVEqfhJul4lqZKtDr8zTqyo3ggWQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 3,
        "relative_time_description": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Store needs better organization and love. Had a lot of promise but now seems to be on a decline with lack of attention.  Still able to find some good stuff.  Bring back a section dedicated to new arrivals in both used and new. If the new store times are right being open only Sat and Sun not a good thing.",
        "time": 1758121110,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Yan Lefebvre",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107439623616124099704/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUb2bEJWuMjFTuKPZJEhAstB9QtTD3DPzaMMY1de-YanPvHWcMq=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "6 months ago",
        "text": "Been there a few times including last weekend. The store was a mess and hard to figure out anything. I asked the clerk at the counter for 2 very popular bands and her reply was a rude  \"i dont know\".... The prices on some albums make no sens. Its sad since its the only record store in the area and the place has potential.",
        "time": 1754387801,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "kayden mayoff",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107865476333926860324/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUMd95CCpaZ_TI522ANiU_uLmgyDnGdxGd-_9vmHy6Kj1uqWb8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "I almost single-handedly keep this place open. It's a great record store, probably the best near Montreal. You can find great quality records in perfect condition, sometimes even still in the plastic, for less than a microwave dinner. They have a great assortment of unknown older albums and popular newer albums. Take a few hours and look around, I'm sure there will be something of value for anyone.",
        "time": 1738720645,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Mike P",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114710137253922788286/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJpRNdjgdhN0Dcf71llqaVW-TlEJzb6tj4B1O2c-U0-m6ji8Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "12 months ago",
        "text": "Friendly service and fair prices. You should plan some time to go through the vinyls as they are not all well organized but you can find some interesting ones if you have patience.",
        "time": 1739996887,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "A.L.",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105527460842021345142/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIUb4FF-a6x3Dtfh-cIRE0_9li4hiHUr3jqGME5uNETiuA1O4c=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "I've given this store a fair shot repeatedly, but I am still disappointed. For the past 2 or 3 years I'd visit the store once in a while (since it is one of few record stores in the area) and sometimes pick up a used record or two. However, with each visit the lack of care put into the store becomes evident. Just recently the store's layout was \"rearranged\", but its issues have remained the same for years.\n\nFor starters, I have doubts anyone involved knows much about the music they are selling. Every album has a Discogs median (or high end) price slapped on, regardless of condition or pressing. Some albums are just outrageously priced (like a molded, water-damaged common April Wine for $15 among many others). I know most places use these prices, but most of the albums are not sleeved, cleaned or given an outer sleeve (and if given an outer sleeve it is most likely heavily worn), including some of the expensive ones on the wall (I would know since I have purchased some before). You'd figure if they are asking higher-end prices that the records would at least be cared for. The bins are packed with a multitude of the same common album (you'll have no trouble finding 10 copies of the same Loggins & Messina or Chris De Burgh album in the same spot) and I always feel like I'm going through the same stock, without price changes, month after month. Even the discount bins they have are tightly packed to the point where flipping through them is impossible...but why would you want to do that anyways since the albums there are not even worthy of a discounted price. The employees, not to blame them, don't do very much even though the store is in dire need of maintenance.\n\nI don't like leaving negative reviews on small businesses but as a client of this store for a few years now it has just become insulting.",
        "time": 1715824254,
        "translated": false
      }
    ],
